SUMMARY: Toronto Country Fest: Gregory Child's & Heart Lung
DESCRIPTION:Gregory Childs & Heart Lung are a Toronto alt-country\, roots
 \, and rock ’n’ roll band with a sound Alan Cross described as “unplugged
  Nirvana” and “dark Fleetwood Mac” when he featured them in The Edge 102.
 1’s Undiscovered Gem series. A regular presence in Toronto’s music scene\
 , the band plays rooms including the Cameron House\, Dakota Tavern\, and 
 Horseshoe Tavern. On July 17\, they released their self-titled debut albu
 m\, showcasing a blend of alt-country\, folk\, and red-dirt roots rock. T
 hey currently hold a monthly residency at Rod\, Gun & Barbers in the Junc
 tion\, playing the last Saturday of every month.
