SUMMARY: Toronto Country Fest: Darcy Windover & Clayton Yates
DESCRIPTION:There is something dazzling - beguiling even - about the musi
 c of Darcy Windover. Standing at the crossroads of Americana\, roots-rock
 \, folk and country\, the Toronto-based singer/songwriter and admitted ge
 ar nerd is that rarest of musicians\, one whose songs are at once instant
 ly accessible yet utterly unique. His songs charge along like a freight t
 rain\, while the ballads are heartfelt and anthemic. Darcy is joined by C
 layton Yates\, a staple in Canada's roots scene on guitar and mandolin\, 
 and featured in such groups as The Mahones\, The Empty Glasses\, and coun
 tless others.
