SUMMARY: Truth & Reconciliation: An Evening of Reflection
DESCRIPTION:Join Anishnawbe Health Foundation for an evening of reflectio
 n\, learning and connection ahead of the National Day for Truth and Recon
 ciliation.\n\nTogether\, we will gather at the Distillery District to lis
 ten\, learn and reflect on the histories and ongoing impacts of residenti
 al schools and what reconciliation asks of each of us today.\n\nThe eveni
 ng will include words from Indigenous leaders and community voices\, alon
 g with traditional song and Jingle Dress dancing\, creating space to come
  together in community and deepen our understanding of Truth and Reconcil
 iation.\n\nAs we approach September 30\, Anishnawbe Health Foundation inv
 ites you to wear orange and continue your learning beyond this gathering.
  This year’s Anishnawbe Health Foundation Orange Shirt features Held in C
 are\, a design by Indigenous artist Joshua Hunt\, with proceeds supportin
 g Anishnawbe Health Toronto.\n\nPurchase your orange shirt here. https://
 oldscoolgeneralstore.square.site/product/pre-order-orange-shirt-day/3B2R5
 NGCS22L2ORD5ZRFSQXW?cp=true&sa=true&sbp=false&q=false Click here to learn
  more. https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/truth-reconciliation-an-evening-of-ref
 lection-tickets-1999390255075
